WEBVTT

NOTE Only the opening screen is an actual application screenshot. Other visuals are labeled illustrations or account instructions, not acceptance recordings.

1
00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.390
Welcome to Genesis: Juris Studio.

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:10.350
In ten minutes, we will follow a canonical case from import to review and reporting, then start a new case.

3
00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:13.240
This is a narrated, illustrated walkthrough.

4
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:20.880
The opening screen shows the application; clearly labeled instruction segments explain account features that were not recorded.

5
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:25.175
Use fictional or de-identified material when you practise.

6
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:35.620
Choose Demo when you want to learn from a completed example such as Project Canopy.

7
00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:39.560
Its Practice cases link opens the simulation catalogue.

8
00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:43.740
Choose Templates when you want a starting structure for your own case.

9
00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:48.905
A template opens a new draft with an intake prompt; you must supply and review its facts.

10
00:00:49.065 --> 00:00:52.595
Neither action creates an approved organization record.

11
00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:06.995
Our example is Five Flats, Three Borders, sometimes called Five Flats, Three Countries.

12
00:01:07.155 --> 00:01:12.075
Use the complete final Markdown file, including its embedded case data.

13
00:01:12.235 --> 00:01:15.620
From the entry screen, choose Import case or prompt.

14
00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:21.775
Inside the editor, the equivalent route is More actions, then Import case prompt, dot m d.

15
00:01:21.935 --> 00:01:25.135
Importing text is not yet applying its graph.

16
00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:32.955
Choose Verify canonical case.

17
00:01:33.115 --> 00:01:39.355
This path checks the embedded structure and fingerprint locally, without asking AI to reinterpret the file.

18
00:01:39.515 --> 00:01:44.365
Review the verified title, version, twenty-three nodes and thirty-six relations.

19
00:01:44.525 --> 00:01:48.020
A matching fingerprint confirms which case data you have.

20
00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:54.855
It does not independently verify the evidence, legal conclusions, tax rates or any claimed review date.

21
00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:05.585
When the verified preview matches your intended file, choose Apply exact case.

22
00:02:05.745 --> 00:02:09.430
Studio reconstructs that graph and opens the working draft.

23
00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:16.310
Follow the six steps: Brief, Draft review, Facts and evidence, Decision map, Test, and Finish.

24
00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:19.720
The progress indicator describes filled sections.

25
00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:24.265
It does not mean every assumption is proven or that the draft has been saved.

26
00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:35.000
Read the title, jurisdiction, professional role and Case context.

27
00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:42.030
This fictional matter concerns a PRC-resident client, five English flats and a proposed Liechtenstein structure.

28
00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:46.955
The client's preferred structure is a request to investigate, not the answer.

29
00:02:47.115 --> 00:02:51.550
Keep alternative routes, unresolved questions and stop conditions visible.

30
00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:56.210
Preserve the original file before changing its reviewed working copy.

31
00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:03.495
Inspect the evidence and the decision it supports.

32
00:03:03.655 --> 00:03:09.000
For example, the KYC questionnaire connects to the ownership and funds investigation.

33
00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:13.940
A named evidence node is not proof that its underlying document has been accepted.

34
00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:19.585
Record what the source establishes, what remains uncertain, and which decision depends on it.

35
00:03:19.745 --> 00:03:23.600
Use case actions to return directly to missing information.

36
00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:34.225
Review the current file's economics rather than an older demo.

37
00:03:34.385 --> 00:03:44.095
It specifies a one-million-pound price, eight hundred thousand pounds of debt, seven-point-five percent interest and a one-hundred-and-twenty-month amortizing term.

38
00:03:44.255 --> 00:03:49.080
Gross annual rent is two hundred and forty-nine thousand, six hundred pounds.

39
00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:55.665
Check repayment basis, operating costs and structure costs before interpreting any displayed result.

40
00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:03.980
The requested ten-percent return needs a named measure.

41
00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:09.390
Gross yield, cash-on-cash return and equity I R R answer different questions.

42
00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:13.765
Compare the displayed calculations with their assumptions and source evidence.

43
00:04:13.925 --> 00:04:19.390
This file contains provisional acquisition costs and unverified tax-rate sources.

44
00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:26.000
We are demonstrating the review workflow, not confirming a tax advantage or promising that the target is achieved.

45
00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:33.395
Open Decision map and select a decision.

46
00:04:33.555 --> 00:04:38.445
Read the node detail, then follow its connections to the next question or outcome.

47
00:04:38.605 --> 00:04:43.625
In this case, defining the return metric and checking lawful funding are meaningful gates.

48
00:04:43.785 --> 00:04:47.815
Follow a stop or renegotiation route as well as a proceeding route.

49
00:04:47.975 --> 00:04:52.090
A useful map explains why different evidence can change the decision.

50
00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:03.645
Choose Test and read the checks for this case type.

51
00:05:03.805 --> 00:05:09.935
A playable case needs intentional routes and outcomes; Test this case opens its simulation when ready.

52
00:05:10.095 --> 00:05:13.125
Other decision packages use completeness checks.

53
00:05:13.285 --> 00:05:18.455
If an action identifies a missing field or connection, open it and correct the draft.

54
00:05:18.615 --> 00:05:24.170
A successful structural test does not replace evidence review or professional judgment.

55
00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:32.885
Choose Create analytical report.

56
00:05:33.045 --> 00:05:40.920
The Create case report dialog offers Preview PDF and Download PDF, with further options under Report settings and approval.

57
00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:43.350
Begin with an internal review draft.

58
00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:49.285
Inspect its case identity, assumptions, evidence register and portrait decision map.

59
00:05:49.445 --> 00:05:55.450
Downloading a preliminary report does not create independent approval or a governed report in My cases.

60
00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:06.505
After choosing Download PDF, check your browser's downloads and open the file yourself.

61
00:06:06.665 --> 00:06:11.395
The message PDF download started confirms initiation, not delivery.

62
00:06:11.555 --> 00:06:18.720
To preserve an editable canonical handoff, use More actions, then Export Final case prompt, dot m d.

63
00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:21.390
Read its status controls carefully.

64
00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:27.640
A filename containing Final does not supply missing evidence or create independent reviewer approval.

65
00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:35.110
This account workflow is an instruction, not a recorded successful save.

66
00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:40.725
With supported sign-in, Save to workspace stores a Studio draft under your account.

67
00:06:40.885 --> 00:06:45.275
Reopen it through Open saved Studio drafts and check the restored content.

68
00:06:45.435 --> 00:06:48.405
Organization cases in My cases are separate.

69
00:06:48.565 --> 00:06:54.610
If a save is uncertain, preserve your export and investigate before repeating a potentially completed write.

70
00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:03.090
Now create your own fictional case.

71
00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:07.835
Preserve the current work first, return to Case Studio and choose Create a case.

72
00:07:07.995 --> 00:07:11.995
Read any replacement or unsaved-work prompt before proceeding.

73
00:07:12.155 --> 00:07:14.930
The new draft starts a separate authoring task.

74
00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:24.255
Alternatively, choose a suitable starter in Templates; review its case type and intake questions instead of treating the starter as a finished example.

75
00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:38.330
In Brief, describe who is involved, the decision required, the jurisdiction, known facts, available evidence and the deadline.

76
00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:44.190
For practice, ask whether a fictional business should approve a supplier change before a planned launch.

77
00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:48.205
Mark prices and delivery claims as unverified until supported.

78
00:07:48.365 --> 00:07:53.135
State the alternatives and the conditions that would make you pause rather than proceed.

79
00:08:00.650 --> 00:08:05.660
This optional AI path is an instruction, not a recorded authenticated request.

80
00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:10.735
Where enabled, Understand with AI requires sign-in and a confirmed profile.

81
00:08:10.895 --> 00:08:14.340
It proposes changes for review before you apply them.

82
00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:18.125
Check the current data-handling notice before sending material.

83
00:08:18.285 --> 00:08:26.835
If unavailable, continue with manual editing or the explicitly labeled local fallback; do not mistake fallback output for AI analysis.

84
00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:35.665
For the new draft, complete Facts and evidence, then build or review the Decision map.

85
00:08:35.825 --> 00:08:40.295
Give nodes concrete titles and connect each choice to a reasoned next step.

86
00:08:40.455 --> 00:08:44.175
Add the missing evidence instead of writing an unsupported conclusion.

87
00:08:44.335 --> 00:08:53.210
Use Test to find structural gaps, then Finish to choose a report, workspace save or expert-review submission when its requirements are met.

88
00:09:00.650 --> 00:09:07.350
Creating a shared organization record is a separate authenticated workflow, described here rather than recorded.

89
00:09:07.510 --> 00:09:11.875
Select the intended organization, open My cases and choose New case.

90
00:09:12.035 --> 00:09:17.395
Create a pilot matter asks for Title, Jurisdiction, Classification and Priority.

91
00:09:17.555 --> 00:09:22.370
After creation, verify the returned case before adding documents and reviews.

92
00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:28.050
Importing a canonical Studio file alone does not create this organization record.

93
00:09:30.650 --> 00:09:40.720
Your practice task is to import and verify the canonical file, explain one evidence-dependent decision, inspect a draft report, and start a new fictional case.

94
00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:42.965
Preserve the work you want to keep.

95
00:09:43.125 --> 00:09:47.880
Return to Help and guides for chapter links, instructions and troubleshooting.

96
00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:55.415
You have learned the workflow; reliable evidence, confirmed saves and appropriate review determine when a real case is ready.
